ccurate."},"802":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql-25","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql#slow-query-warnings-step","content":"Slow queries may not indicate a database issue (e.g. server hitches)."},"803":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql-26","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql#slow-query-warnings-step","content":"Slow queries on server startup are not necessarily problematic."},"804":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql-27","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql#debug-step","content":"Enabling the debug option will print all queries in the server console; you can also use an array to only print from a list of resources instead."},"805":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql-28","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql#debug-step","content":"You can temporarily modify the resource list with commands."},"806":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql-29","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql#compatibility","content":"You can delete the following resources and allow oxmysql to provide their functionality."},"807":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql-30","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql#compatibility","content":"mysql-async"},"808":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql-31","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql#compatibility","content":"ghmattimysql"},"809":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql-32","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql#usage","content":"Resources can import oxmysql methods by including our library, granting some type-checking and minor performance improvements over raw export calls."},"810":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql-33","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql#lua","content":"Modify `fxmanifest.lua` for your resource, and add the following above any other script files."},"811":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql-34","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql#javascript","content":"You can use raw exports, or install our npm package for intellisense and similar usage as Lua."},"812":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql-35","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql#javascript","content":"Import the oxmysql object into your resource."},"813":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql-36","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql#upserting","content":"When uncertain if a row should be inserted into the database, or an existing row should be updated, queries should check for duplicate keys."},"814":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql-37","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql#upserting","content":"This is preferred over checking the existence of a row, then inserting or updating depending on the result.\\\nFurthermore, unlike using 'REPLACE INTO', the row is not deleted and re-inserted."},"815":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql/placeholders","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql/placeholders","type":"page","content":"Placeholders","breadcrumbs":["Docs","OxMySQL"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/oxmysql/placeholders"},"816":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql/placeholders-0","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql/placeholders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql/placeholders","content":"Placeholders allow for query parameters to be safely executed, preventing common SQL injection methods."},"817":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql/placeholders-1","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql/placeholders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql/placeholders","content":"Parameters can be passed an an array or object (referred to as named parameters)."},"818":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql/placeholders-2","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql/placeholders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql/placeholders","content":"These are distinct from prepared statements which are handled by the MySQL server; you can use `MySQL.prepare` for more optimised and secure queries."},"819":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql/ui","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql/ui","type":"page","content":"Using the Debug UI","breadcrumbs":["Docs","OxMySQL"],"tags":[